## 2. Flutter Architecture Design

### 2.1 Recommended Pattern: Clean Architecture + Feature-First

Your current FSD maps well to Flutter's Clean Architecture:

| React (Current) | Flutter (Target) | Notes |
|------------------|------------------|-------|
| `src/entities/[entity]/api/` | `lib/features/[entity]/data/` | Data sources, repositories |
| `src/entities/[entity]/model/` | `lib/features/[entity]/domain/` | Use cases, entities |
| `src/entities/[entity]/ui/` | `lib/features/[entity]/presentation/` | Screens, widgets |
| `src/hooks/` | `lib/core/` | Shared utilities |
| `src/services/offline/` | `lib/core/offline/` | Offline engine |
| `src/lib/scoringEngine.ts` | `lib/core/scoring/` | Pure Dart — easiest port |
| `src/components/ui/` | `lib/shared/widgets/` | Design system |

### 2.2 Proposed Directory Structure

```text
lib/
├── app/                          # App initialization, routing, DI
│   ├── app.dart
│   ├── router.dart               # GoRouter or AutoRoute
│   └── di/                       # GetIt / Riverpod providers
├── core/                         # Cross-cutting infrastructure
│   ├── auth/                     # Supabase auth wrapper
│   ├── offline/                  # SQLite sync engine
│   │   ├── database.dart         # Drift/SQLite schema
│   │   ├── outbox.dart           # Mutation queue
│   │   └── sync_engine.dart      # Background sync
│   ├── scoring/                  # Pure Dart scoring engine
│   ├── network/                  # Connectivity monitoring
│   ├── logging/                  # Logger service
│   └── theme/                    # Design tokens, themes
├── features/                     # Domain features (mirrors entities)
│   ├── submission/
│   │   ├── data/                 # Supabase data sources + repos
│   │   ├── domain/               # Entities, use cases
│   │   └── presentation/         # Screens, widgets, state (Bloc/Riverpod)
│   ├── template/
│   ├── store/
│   ├── action_plan/
│   ├── user/
│   ├── notification/
│   ├── ai_assistant/
│   └── analytics/
└── shared/                       # Shared widgets, extensions
    ├── widgets/                  # Buttons, cards, inputs
    └── extensions/               # Dart extensions
```

### 2.3 State Management Recommendation

| Option | Verdict |
|--------|---------|
| **Riverpod** ⭐ | Best for this project. Type-safe, testable, no boilerplate. Natural replacement for TanStack Query's `useQuery`/`useMutation` pattern |
| **Bloc** | More verbose but excellent for complex state machines (audit form). Good if team prefers explicit event/state modeling |
| **Provider** | Too basic for this complexity |

> **Recommendation**: Use **Riverpod** as primary state management. It has a `ref.watch()` / `ref.read()` pattern that maps naturally to your React Query hooks.

