## 5. Supabase-Flutter Integration

The `supabase_flutter` package provides near-identical APIs to the JS client:

```dart
// Initialize (main.dart)
await Supabase.initialize(
  url: 'YOUR_SUPABASE_URL',
  anonKey: 'YOUR_ANON_KEY',
  authOptions: const FlutterAuthClientOptions(
    authFlowType: AuthFlowType.pkce,
  ),
);

// Auth — same as JS
final session = supabase.auth.currentSession;
await supabase.auth.signInWithPassword(email: email, password: password);

// Queries — same as JS  
final data = await supabase
    .from('submissions')
    .select('*, answers(*)')
    .eq('store_id', storeId);

// Realtime — same as JS
supabase
    .channel('notifications')
    .onPostgresChanges(
      event: PostgresChangeEvent.insert,
      schema: 'public',
      table: 'notifications',
      filter: PostgresChangeFilter(type: PostgresChangeFilterType.eq, column: 'user_id', value: userId),
      callback: (payload) => handleNotification(payload),
    )
    .subscribe();

// Storage — same as JS
await supabase.storage.from('audit-photos').upload(path, file);
```

> [!NOTE]
> **RLS policies, Edge Functions, and database triggers remain 100% unchanged.** The entire backend is reusable. Only the client changes.

