## 6. Internal Distribution Strategy

Since you're not publishing to public app stores, here are your options:

### 6.1 iOS Distribution

| Method | Setup Effort | Auto-Update | Cost | Best For |
|--------|-------------|-------------|------|----------|
| **TestFlight** ⭐ | Low | ✅ Yes | $99/yr (Apple Dev) | Your use case — up to 10,000 testers |
| **Apple Enterprise Program** | High (requires DUNS) | ✅ Via MDM | $299/yr | Companies with 100+ devices, MDM |
| **Ad Hoc** | Medium | ❌ No | $99/yr | <100 devices, manual install |

> **Recommendation**: **TestFlight** is perfect. 10,000 testers, automatic updates, no App Store review for internal builds. Just upload via Xcode or CI.

### 6.2 Android Distribution

| Method | Setup Effort | Auto-Update | Cost | Best For |
|--------|-------------|-------------|------|----------|
| **Firebase App Distribution** ⭐ | Low | ✅ Yes (via tester app) | Free | Your use case |
| **Direct APK / App Bundle** | Minimal | ❌ Manual | Free | Quick testing |
| **Google Play Internal Testing** | Low | ✅ Yes | $25 one-time | If you want Play Store infra |

> **Recommendation**: **Firebase App Distribution** for Android. Free, supports groups, and auto-notifies testers of new builds.

### 6.3 OTA Updates (Hot Reload in Production)

| Tool | Description | Cost |
|------|-------------|------|
| **Shorebird** ⭐ | Dart-level code push. Update without re-deploying | Free for small teams |
| **CodePush (MS)** | React Native only — N/A | — |

> [!TIP]
> **Shorebird** lets you push Dart code updates to deployed Flutter apps without going through TestFlight/Firebase again. This gives you the same "instant update" experience your PWA currently has via Service Workers.

