## 7. Phased Migration Roadmap

### Phase 1: Foundation (2-3 weeks)

- [ ] Flutter project scaffold with Clean Architecture
- [ ] Supabase integration (`supabase_flutter`)
- [ ] Auth flow (Login, Session persistence, RBAC guard)
- [ ] Navigation shell (GoRouter with role-based guards)
- [ ] Design system (Theme tokens, shared widgets)
- [ ] CI/CD pipeline (GitHub Actions → TestFlight + Firebase App Distribution)

### Phase 2: Core Audit Flow (3-4 weeks)

- [ ] Template list + detail viewer
- [ ] Store selector
- [ ] Audit form (criteria rendering, answer capture, photo picker)
- [ ] Scoring engine port (pure Dart — test-driven)
- [ ] GPS verification
- [ ] Submission flow (online path)

### Phase 3: Offline Engine (3-4 weeks)

- [ ] Drift database schema (mirrors Dexie)
- [ ] Read-path caching (templates, stores, profile)
- [ ] Transactional outbox (mutation queue)
- [ ] Sync engine with connectivity monitoring
- [ ] Photo blob persistence + sync
- [ ] Airplane Reboot Test verification

### Phase 4: Secondary Features (2-3 weeks)

- [ ] Action Plan management
- [ ] Dashboard with charts (`fl_chart`)
- [ ] Notifications (realtime + push via FCM)
- [ ] Dark mode / theme switching

### Phase 5: Polish & Distribution (1-2 weeks)

- [ ] TestFlight setup + first iOS build
- [ ] Firebase App Distribution setup + first Android build
- [ ] Shorebird integration for OTA updates
- [ ] Performance profiling (DevTools)
- [ ] User acceptance testing

**Total Estimated Timeline: 11-16 weeks** (1 developer, full-time)

---

## 8. Risk Assessment

| Risk | Severity | Mitigation |
|------|----------|------------|
| **Full rewrite — no code reuse** | 🔴 High | Scoring engine is pure logic → direct port. Supabase API calls are nearly identical. Focus rewrite effort on UI layer |
| **Two codebases to maintain** | 🔴 High | Consider sunsetting the PWA once Flutter app is stable. Or use Flutter Web to serve both |
| **iOS signing / provisioning** | 🟡 Medium | Apple Developer account required ($99/yr). TestFlight simplifies distribution |
| **Team needs to learn Dart** | 🟡 Medium | Dart is very similar to TypeScript. Most devs ramp up in 1-2 weeks |
| **Offline complexity doubles** | 🔴 High | Drift (SQLite) is more reliable than IndexedDB. Patterns are the same, implementation is different |
| **Flutter Web as alternative** | 🟡 Info | Flutter can target web too. Possible to maintain ONE codebase for both mobile and web. Trade-off: Flutter web performance and SEO are weaker than React |

---

## 9. Alternative: Flutter Web (Single Codebase)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Before committing to a mobile-only Flutter app, consider **Flutter Web**. This would let you replace the React PWA entirely and have ONE codebase for both mobile apps (TestFlight/APK) and web (admin dashboard).

| Pro | Con |
|-----|-----|
| Single codebase for iOS + Android + Web | Flutter Web performance is worse than React |
| Native camera/GPS on mobile, web fallback on desktop | Flutter Web SEO is poor (not relevant for internal app) |
| Unified design language | Flutter Web rendering can feel "non-native" on browsers |
| One team, one language (Dart) | Admin-heavy features (Template Builder) may be awkward |

**Verdict**: For an internal-only app with no SEO concerns, Flutter Web is a viable path. The Template Builder's drag-and-drop complexity is the main risk.

