## 10. Team & Skill Requirements

| Skill | Current Team Has? | Action |
|-------|-------------------|--------|
| **Dart / Flutter** | Probably No | 1-2 weeks ramp-up for TS devs |
| **Supabase** | ✅ Yes | API is nearly identical in Dart |
| **SQLite / Drift** | Probably No | 1 week learning Drift ORM |
| **iOS Provisioning** | Maybe | Apple Dev account + Xcode required |
| **CI/CD (Fastlane/GH Actions)** | Maybe | Templated pipelines available |

---

## 11. Recommended Next Steps

1. **Decision Gate**: Do you want **mobile-only Flutter** or **Flutter Web** (single codebase for everything)?
2. **Proof of Concept**: Build a minimal Flutter app with Supabase auth + one offline audit submission (2-3 days)
3. **Approve Phase 1**: If POC validates, proceed with the Phase 1 Foundation sprint
4. **Parallel Operation**: Keep the PWA running during migration. Cut over when Flutter reaches feature parity on Tier 1

---

> **Scout's Closing Note**: This is a significant investment (~3-4 months for one developer). The payoff is real — native camera, reliable GPS, true background sync, and unlimited offline storage solve the exact pain points your field auditors face with the PWA. The backend (Supabase, RLS, Edge Functions, triggers) is 100% reusable. The rewrite cost is entirely in the UI and offline engine layers.
